{"defs":{},"properties":[{"path":["mediaType"],"schema_type":"string"},{"path":["encoding"],"schema_type":"string"},{"path":["schema"]},{"path":["collection"],"description":"The URI of the OGC API collection that should be accessed to provide input values\nfrom the corresponding process input. The server offering this collection is\nreferred to as the \"value source server\".","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["bbox"],"description":"Only resources that have a geometry that intersects the bounding box are selected. The\nbounding box is provided as four or six numbers, depending on whether the coordinate\nreference system includes a vertical axis. If the value consists of four numbers, the\ncoordinate reference system is WGS84 longitude/latitude\n(http://www.opengis.net/def/crs/OGC/1.3/CRS84) unless a different coordinate reference\nsystem is specified in the parameter `bboxCrs`. If the value consists of six numbers,\nthe coordinate reference system is WGS84 (http://www.opengis.net/def/crs/OGC/0/CRS84h)\nlongitude/latitude/ellipsoidal height unless a different coordinate reference system is\nspecified in the parameter `bboxCrs`.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["bboxCrs"],"description":"Asserts the CRS used for the coordinate values of the `bbox` parameter. The default is\nWGS 84 or WGS84h depending on whether ellipsoidal height is included or not.","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["geometry"],"description":"Only resources that have a geometry that intersects the geometry specified using the\n`geometry` parameter are selected. The value of the `geometry` parameter can be\nspecified using WKT or GeoJSON.","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["geometryCrs"],"description":"Asserts the CRS used for the coordinate values of the `geometry` parameter. The default\nis WGS 84 or WGS84h depending on whether ellipsoidal height is included or not.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["datetime"],"description":"Either a date-time or an interval, half-bounded or bounded. Date and time expressions\nadhere to RFC 3339. Half-bounded intervals are expressed using double-dots. Examples:\na date-time (\"2018-02-12T23:20:50Z\"), a bounded interval\n(\"2018-02-12T00:00:00Z/2018-03-18T12:31:12Z\"), or half-bounded intervals\n(\"2018-02-12T00:00:00Z/..\" or \"../2018-03-18T12:31:12Z\"). Only resources that have a\ntemporal property that intersects the value of `datetime` are selected.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["limit"],"description":"The optional limit parameter limits the number of items that are presented in the\nresponse document. Only items on the first level of the collection are counted.","schema_type":"integer","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["crs"],"description":"If specified, the coordinates of all geometry-valued properties in the response\ndocument are in the requested CRS. Otherwise the coordinates are in the default CRS.","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["filter"],"description":"A search or filter condition determining which resources from the OGC API collection\nare included in the result set and thus passed as values to the corresponding process\ninput. Can be a string in a text-based query language (e.g. cql2-text) or a CQL2 JSON\nobject.","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["filterCrs"],"description":"Asserts the CRS used for the coordinate values of the `filter` parameter. The default\nis WGS 84 or WGS84h depending on whether ellipsoidal height is included or not.","schema_type":"string","format":"uri-reference","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["filterLang"],"description":"Indicates the language used to encode a filter expression specified using the `filter`\nparameter.","schema_type":"string","enum":["cql2-text","cql2-json","fes-xml"],"sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["subset"],"description":"Retrieve only part of the data by slicing or trimming along one or more axis. For\ntrimming: `{axisAbbrev}({low}:{high})` (preserves dimensionality). An asterisk (`*`) can\nbe used instead of `{low}` or `{high}` to indicate the minimum/maximum value. For\nslicing: `{axisAbbrev}({value})` (reduces dimensionality).","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["subsetCrs"],"description":"Asserts the CRS used for the coordinate values of the `subset` parameter. The default\nis WGS 84 or WGS84h depending on whether ellipsoidal height is included or not.","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["ids"],"description":"Allows a specific list of resources, indicated by their identifiers, to be fetched from\nthe OGC API collection. Only resources whose identifier matches one of the listed\nvalues shall appear in the result set.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["q"],"description":"Supports keyword searching. Only resources whose text fields contain one or more of the\nspecified search terms are selected.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["assets"],"description":"A list of STAC asset tags.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["properties"],"description":"A filter that selects resource properties to be included in a response document. The\nelements can be the names of resource properties, aliases for resource properties, or\nsynthetic properties.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["aliases"],"description":"A dictionary of aliases that can be used as values for the `properties` parameter.\nAliases can be alternative names for resource properties or synthetic properties\ncomputed at run-time using an expression language.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["passThroughParameters"],"description":"Parameters specified in this object are passed through to the value source server for\nprocessing on that server. The keys should match query parameters that the value source\nserver recognizes.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://ogc.api.processes.part2.schemas.collectionValue"]},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","1"],"title":"a","keyword":"branch"},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","1","args"],"required":true,"schema_type":"array"},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","1","op"],"required":true,"schema_type":"string","enum":["accenti"]},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","0","args"],"required":true,"schema_type":"array"},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf"],"keyword":"oneOf"},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","2"],"title":"b","keyword":"branch"},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","2","args"],"required":true,"schema_type":"array"},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","0","args","_oneOf","2","args","_oneOf"],"keyword":"oneOf"},{"path":["filter","_oneOf","1","_oneOf","2","_oneOf